# i18n

User-visible strings in `packages/app` and `packages/landing` use `t()` from `$lib/i18n`. The **English sentence is the key**. Locales: `en`, `es`, `ko` in `packages/i18n/locales/`.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import { useI18n } from '$lib/i18n';

	const { t } = useI18n();
</script>

<button>{t('Save')}</button>
<p>{t('{count} matches', { count })}</p>
```

```json
// en.json / es.json / ko.json — same key in all three
"Save": "Save",
"{count} matches": "{count} matches"
```

- Add the key to **en.json, es.json, and ko.json**. Translate es/ko; if unsure, copy English so the key exists.
- Params are `{name}` in the key, passed as `{ name }` to `t()`.
- `packages/ui` stays English (default props). App/landing hosts pass `t('…')` when wrapping.
- App: module singleton (`ssr = false`). Landing: per-request instance on `locals` (never a module singleton). Server actions/errors use `locals.t`.
- Landing URLs: English stays unprefixed (`/players`). Spanish/Korean use `/es/...` and `/ko/...`. `/en/...` 301s to the unprefixed path. Wire internal links with `localizeHref` / `href()`. Do not auto-redirect from `Accept-Language`.
- Do not hardcode UI copy in app or landing routes/components. Do not invent a second i18n system.
